  "task_description": "Binary classification of tiny synthetic 4-feature vectors. Each sample is\nx in R^4 drawn uniformly from [-1, 1]; the label is 1 exactly when\nx0*x1 + sin(pi*x2) > x3, with 3% of labels deterministically flipped, so a\nperfect score is impossible by construction. The golden metric is accuracy\nover the held-out evaluation rows and HIGHER is better. The dataset is\n256 rows in 4 shards, regenerated bit-identically from a pinned seed \u2014\nthis task exists to demonstrate the SIDERIUS workflow mechanics on a CPU\nin seconds, not to be a benchmark.",
